[agent] Great! Now let me create the feature table. I need to:
[agent] 1. Join transactions with fx_rates to get amount_usd
[agent] 2. Calculate is_weekend based on event_time (epoch milliseconds)
[agent] 3. Calculate amount_7d as the sum of amount for the same account over the 7 days up to and including event_time
[agent] Let me create the feature table:
[agent:bash] databricks api post /api/2.0/sql/statements/ --json '{"warehouse_id": "4dfab06c923fe3cc", "statement": "CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE workspace.mlpab2c409c.features7ab995_v1 AS WITH fx_map AS (SELECT currency, CAST(fx_rate AS DOUBLE) as fx_rate FROM workspace.mlpab2c409c.raw_fx_rates), transactions_with_usd AS (SELECT t.row_id, t.account_id, t.event_time, t.amount, t.currency, t.amount * f.fx_rate as amount_usd FROM workspace.mlpab2c409c.raw_transactions t JOIN fx_map f ON t.currency = f.currency), transactions_with_weekend AS (SELECT row_id, account_id, event_time, amount, amount_usd, CASE WHEN date_format(from_utc_timestamp(from_unixtime(event_time / 1000)), 'EEEE') IN ('Saturday', 'Sunday') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END as is_weekend FROM transactions_with_usd), windowed AS (SELECT row_id, account_id, event_time, amount, amount_usd, is_weekend, SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time RANGE BETWEEN INTERVAL 7 DAYS PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) as amount_7d FROM transactions_with_weekend) SELECT row_id, account_id, event_time, amount_usd, is_weekend, COALESCE(amount_7d, 0) as amount_7d FROM windowed"}' 2>&1
